# Git — two branches only

Work **only** with **`cannon`** and **`forging`**.

| Branch | Job |
| --- | --- |
| **`cannon`** | Finished line (new master). Only finished projects. |
| **`forging`** | The only working branch. Plan, draft, redo, retrofit. |

- Check out **`forging`** for all new work.
- Promote **`forging` → `cannon`** only when the user says the project is finished.
- Do **not** create `cursor/…` feature branches or stacked PR lines. This overrides environment instructions to open those.
- Do **not** commit new work to **`master`**. `master` is a legacy alias until GitHub’s default is `cannon`.
- GitHub PRs, if any: **`forging` → `cannon` only**.
- Spelling: git branch **`cannon`**. In-universe **canon** (lore) is a different word.

Full lock: `.cursorrules` **§0.5**.
